[%-
	url = '/';
	title = 'STACKIT Compute Engine Pricing & Instance Type Comparison';
	description = 'Compare all STACKIT Compute Engine instance types across both regions (eu01, eu02). Filter by family, hardware (Intel, AMD, ARM, GPU) and compare Single-AZ and Multi-AZ pricing.';
-%]
[%- PROCESS include_header.tt2 -%]

<h1>STACKIT Compute Engine Pricing</h1>

<p>
Struggling to pick the right STACKIT Compute Engine instance type?
This webapp consolidates the public STACKIT price list into one searchable place,
so you can compare vCPU, memory, hardware and price across both STACKIT regions
without hopping between docs.
</p>

<h2>Instance Types</h2>

<p>
Explore <a href="/instances.html">[% instances.size %] STACKIT Compute Engine instance types</a> at a glance!
Filter by family
(<a href="/compute-optimized.html">Compute Optimized</a>,
<a href="/general-purpose.html">General Purpose</a>,
<a href="/memory-optimized.html">Memory Optimized</a>,
<a href="/tiny.html">Tiny</a>,
<a href="/gpu.html">GPU</a>)
or by hardware
(<a href="/intel.html">Intel</a>,
<a href="/amd.html">AMD</a>,
<a href="/arm.html">ARM</a>).
</p>

<h2>Regions</h2>

<p>
STACKIT currently runs <a href="/regions.html">[% regions.size %] regions</a> in the European Union:
[%- FOREACH region IN regions %]
<a href="/[% region.region %].html"><code>[% region.region %]</code></a> ([% region.regionName %])[% UNLESS loop.last %],[% END %]
[%- END -%].
Each region offers a Single-AZ and a Multi-AZ (metro, <code>-m</code>) availability tier.
</p>

<h2>Block Storage</h2>

<p>
Compare <a href="/block-storage.html">STACKIT Block Storage pricing</a> too:
capacity volumes and backups billed per GB, plus fixed performance classes
(billed per disk) with defined IOPS and throughput &mdash; across both regions
and availability tiers.
</p>

<h2>Instance Picker</h2>

<p>
The powerful <a href="/picker.html">Instance Picker</a> lets you compare every
STACKIT instance type across regions with granular, sortable filters on vCPU, memory,
hardware, architecture and price.
</p>

<h2>About the data</h2>

<p>
Pricing is imported from the public STACKIT Price Information Model (PIM) API
(<code>https://pim.api.stackit.cloud/v1/skus</code>).
Only Compute Engine "Virtual Machines" (including GPU servers) are shown.
Additional details such as exact CPU architecture, CPU model and GPU model are
curated separately and can be extended over time.
</p>

[% PROCESS include_footer.tt2 %]
